Z||000000||MontanaFiero||10-06-2001||02:09 PM||||On my '86 SE with backlit gauges, and a V-6, my temp gauge won't register. There is power to it, because it moves when the key is turned on. I just bought a brand new sensor, and a new plug for it too.<P>If I short across the terminals of the plug, I also get no response from the gauge.<P>any suggestions?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||10-06-2001||05:07 PM||||there are two diff senders one is only for the computer the other is the gauge sender.<BR>does the wires ck ok do you have a V.O.M. to see if you have power to the sender and or the gauge. the start key on jump is not the same as out put reading from the sender!!!<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||10-06-2001||06:48 PM||||Shorting across the 2 terminals on that sender won't do anything. One of the wires is for the idiot light and the other one is for the gage. Try touching both wires to ground (ignition on of course)and the light should light and the gage should peg. If the light and gage both do their thing then the sender is at fault,if not then the problem lays either in the wires or the gage itself. Better add - the gage/light sender is the one in the head by the coil<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 10-06-2001).]||||reg||1
